James sought guidance on submitting a single LaTeX file to a journal requiring unified references, including two bibliographies. I provided a detailed method to combine references using the `bibunits` package, compiling `.bbl` files into the main `.tex` document. Later, James inquired about handling cross-references to his supplementary information (SI) without external `.aux` files due to the single-file requirement. I clarified that he should move the SI content into the main file, use internal labels, and reference them using standard `\ref{}` commands, thus eliminating the need for the `xr` package while ensuring all parts compile correctly within one document.
